// Toward the eye
//
// An object-space offset moving a vertex `distance` metres along its view
// ray towards the eye: where it lands on screen does not change, only how
// deep it is. A decal laid flat on a road that is not quite flat then
// still passes the depth test, while what stands clearly in front of the
// road (a car, its tyres) still hides it: a depth bias in metres.
//
// Original implementation.

fn toward_eye(
    normal_matrix: mat3x3f,
    view: vec3f,       // Towards the eye, world space. @default 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
    distance: f32,     // How far towards the eye, metres. @default 0.25
) -> vec3f {
    return transpose(normal_matrix) * view * distance;
}
